      "id": "note",
      "kind": "edit.markdownNote",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "# SDF Primitives with Timeline\nThis is a copy of the SDF shader workflow. The Timeline sits between the Trackpad-updated JSON state and Metal Render. Its /timeSeconds track uses Ease In/Out to complete one camera orbit and return to the starting view, so the 120-frame clip can loop smoothly. Trackpad X remains a live camera offset. The Timeline controls the 30-fps run through Output → Timeline → Start, and its frame rate feeds Video Output. Select Timeline to edit the track in the bottom panel or preview any frame. Source and MIT license: Examples/SDFPrimitives.metal."
      },
      "resources": {},
      "title": "How the timeline works"
    },
